    "difficulty": 1,
    "marks": 1,
    "estimatedSeconds": 40,
    "stem": "Triangle $ABC$ has a right angle at $B$. Which fraction is equal to $\\sin A$?",
    "options": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "content": "$\\dfrac{BC}{AC}$",
        "correct": true,
        "rationale": "$BC$ is opposite $A$ and $AC$ is the hypotenuse: $\\sin A = \\frac{O}{H}$."
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "content": "$\\dfrac{AB}{AC}$",
        "rationale": "$AB$ is adjacent to $A$, so this is $\\cos A$."
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "content": "$\\dfrac{BC}{AB}$",
        "rationale": "Opposite over adjacent is $\\tan A$."
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "content": "$\\dfrac{AC}{BC}$",
        "rationale": "This is upside down: the hypotenuse belongs on the bottom."
      }
    ],
    "explanation": "Relative to angle $A$: the opposite side is $BC$, the adjacent side is $AB$ and the hypotenuse is $AC$ (opposite the right angle). So $\\sin A = \\frac{BC}{AC}$.",
